Z||000000||Stungbymystang||12-01-2001||02:21 AM||||For those of you that remember, I am the guy that doesn't know jack about these cars but want one. <P>I went and found one for sale on the side of the road for sale. I stopped and looked.<BR>It was an red 87 GT, with air, auto, and 150+K miles. Busted rear quarter window, and bad paint all round. The front of the bumper was cracked. This thing was a beater from hell. But I figuered I could prolly work on it in my spare time. So I call the number. <P>he wants $4,500. This car is completly stock.<BR>A motor that doesn't have a lot of life left and all the before metioned defects. <BR>I almost laughed at the guy!<P>Correct me if I am wrong, because again I know so little. But $4,500 for this car was outrages in my opinion.<P>Oh well. The search goes on.<P>------------------<BR>Check Her Out <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/xvwannabemevx/home.html" TARGET=_blank>Jade Not Your Average 6</A><BR>94, v6 Auto. 144,220 miles (engine rebuilt @ 139,330)<P>Mods:<BR>K&N, Duals w/flowmasters, Mac 1 5/8 headers<BR>Crank Underdrive Pulley<BR>3.73's<BR>JMS Chip <P>Sounds: <BR>Alpine Head Unit<BR>3 Alpine V12's, 1 JL Audio 500/1<BR>2 JL 12's, 2 Kenwood 6x9's, 2 Kenwood 5x7's, 6 Alpine Tweets||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||12-01-2001||02:34 AM||||Ya you were right, some people get confused. From your description it's worth about 5-800 depending on interior.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LoW_KeY||12-01-2001||02:54 AM||||ouch.. 4500 would buy you once nice looking one! that guy probably thinks he can get something because its rare to him.<P>I seen a car dealership guy in my area has a GT thats been sitting outside for 6 months "not for sale" so he's just going to let it rot, so sad...<P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||soup||12-01-2001||03:09 AM||||I payed 4,700 Canadian for my 87 GT with T-Tops, the interior is almost imaculate but they front hood has clear coat pealing, the side sail panels are cracked, and the front fascia is cracked on the bottom passenger side, but I also got a full body with from an 86 SE. <P>So i guess what i am saying is if that is 4,500 american, i think you are getting screwed, from what ive seen on canadatrader.com, 4,500 canadian is still a little high, see if you can take him to 4.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GTMike||12-01-2001||05:08 AM||||i paid 5,000 for mine but its is in show condition  only had 43k miles.  has cruse air power everything and a 5 speed. one owner alwasy garaged.    i had to fly to get it though.  <P>i wouldn't get an auto unless your going to put alot of hp in it.    fieros are best zipping down twisty roads.  its fun to bang some gears  and laying a good patch of rubber.   you wont be able to do that with and auto with an engine that has 150k miles on it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2ndchancefiero||12-01-2001||07:37 AM|||| Way too much..i paid $1500.00 dollars for a red 1987 GT with 105,000miles runs great, no codes, interior mint, just needs a front fascia (has a crack in it) and the hood repainted. Keep looking they are out there.<P>------------------<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||1
