Z||000009||stimpy||12-01-2001||11:43 AM||||That guy is getting high off of his own supply. I paid $2500 for my 86 GT. Sail panels where brittle, but not cracked, body totally straight, and 127,000 miles with a new clutch. No mechanical problems whatsoever, and interior was ok except for the drivers seat. Go ahead, laugh at him.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||12-01-2001||12:14 PM||||I'd say $4500USD was too much if it was stock although I wouldn't worry too much about the mileage.  I have almost 200k on my '86 GT (bottom end rebuilt) and she's still running strong with just a little bit of smoke on startup.  Some of these 2.8s are going close to 300k miles before they give up.<P>Maybe I got taken when I bought my car.  I paid $3400 with 195k miles (bottom end rebuilt), stock but poor condition wheels (one was bent) with no tires (had to bring my own wheels/tires from home), avg interior, avg paint with a few very bad spots, non working stereo, Getrag swapped out for a 4 spd, etc, etc.  I'm not even going to go into my sad story about the attempted trip home.  What a nightmare.  The frustration was worth a grand by itself!<P>Now I have almost 6 grand in a car that's maybe worth $4500 (custom center console, soon to be factory sub system, aftermarket stereo, new tires, etc).  Maybe I'll trade it in for something else.  Just about time to move on.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Jay||12-01-2001||12:14 PM||||I paid $500 for my 86 GT and it was in terrible shape.  The interior looked like it was black it was so dirty.  I ripped it out and put in a new one.  $4500 US is too much, for a little bit more you could by mine <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598567222" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598567222</A> <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Peachez||12-01-2001||12:54 PM||||i bought my 84 2m4 for $600.  had been sitting for 7 years so the tires were egg shaped and it didn't have an engine as well as the cables were cut.  thats all that was wrong with it though.  great body, great interior paint still in good shape.  i ended up putting a jasper rebuilt high performance 4 cylinder in it as well as spent alot more money fixing things up for personal reasons.  nonetheless 2000 even for that description is too high.  i dont know what kind of stunt he is trying to pull.  i know im not going to get NEAR what i put into my car when i sell it in years to come and its almost in mint condition.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Raydar||12-01-2001||12:57 PM||||Here's what $4500 US will get you. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.autotrader.com/findacar/vdetail.jtmpl?car_id=71049269&dealer_id=&certified=n&max_price=&start_year=1988&end_year=1988&address=30134&search_type=used&make=PONT&model=FIER" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autotrader.com/findacar/vdetail.jtmpl?car_id=71049269&dealer_id=&certified=n&max_price=&start_year=1988&end_year=1988&address=30134&search_type=used&make=PONT&model=FIER</A>  O&min_price=&distance=200&advcd_on=n&advanced=n&car_year=1988&ac_afflt=ATLANTACLASSIFIEDS.COM<P>I've seen this car. It's beautiful. Belongs to Jason Maples in Huntsville. If I had the money, I'd be there in a heartbeat.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><P>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-01-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
